tools/evals/bench_prompts/*siting*
# national sweep + its baseline (2026-07-30): a private-engine regression harness — it imports
# dail_tracker_core.siting, so it cannot run from a public clone. These two were tracked publicly
# by oversight and were the 2 paths tools/check_no_private_ip.py blocked on.
tools/siting_national_sweep.py
data/_meta/siting_national_sweep_baseline.json

# === THE CONSOLIDATION TARGET (2026-07-31) — see doc/private/PLAN_PLANNING_CONSOLIDATION.md ===
# Every pattern above this line is a hand-maintained glob, and every siting leak on record came
# from one that did not descend into a subdirectory. As the engine moves into planning/product/,
# this single prefix replaces them: a directory prefix needs no negation and cannot miss a new
# file. Added BEFORE the first file lands there, so nothing is ever briefly visible to `git add -A`.
# planning/civic/ is the deliberately-PUBLIC sibling — never add it here.
/planning/product/

# Commercial product applications and their private integration modules are kept out of this
# PUBLIC repository. `/apps/public-signal/` is the whole boundary: it is a directory prefix, so a
# new private file is covered by default rather than by someone remembering to list it.
#
# CONSOLIDATED 2026-08-08. PublicSignal's composition modules used to live at
# dail_tracker_core/queries/procurement/{opportunities,market_intel}.py with their tests under
# test/, versioned by a separate .git-publicsignal overlay because git cannot track files above a
# repo's root. They now live at apps/public-signal/private-api/psintel/ and .../tests/, and the
# overlay is retired. That list-of-files approach had already failed once: market_intel.py was
# added to this file but NOT to tools/check_no_private_ip.py's DENY_EXACT, so one of the two
# guards did not know it was private.
#
# The individual entries below are now dead paths - nothing exists there. They are KEPT
# deliberately: they cost nothing, and if a file is ever recreated at one of those paths it stays
# private instead of silently becoming public. Do not "tidy" them away.
/apps/planspec-demo/
/apps/public-signal/
/test/apps/
# A retired overlay is a whole git OBJECT DATABASE, so committing one embeds that repo's entire
# history inside this PUBLIC one — bloat is the lesser problem. Added 2026-08-08 after a broad
# `git add` swept 1,714 files / 98 MB of .git-publicsignal.RETIRED-2026-08-08 into a commit.
# Caught before the push. The glob covers any future retirement, not just that one date.
/.git-publicsignal.RETIRED-*/
/.git-*.RETIRED-*/
/dail_tracker_core/queries/procurement/opportunities.py
/dail_tracker_core/queries/procurement/market_intel.py
/test/api/test_api_publicsignal_feed.py
/test/dail_tracker_core/test_publicsignal_opportunities.py
/test/dail_tracker_core/test_publicsignal_market_intel.py

# Node dependencies — installed via npm, never tracked (added 2026-08-01 after
# node_modules/axe-core was committed by accident in 39bda48 "planning features").
node_modules/

# Rebuildable sandbox aggregation cache; retain its generator and reviewed findings.
/pipeline_sandbox/disclosed_po_spend/agg.pkl
